The thread-state registry (C7 (b); rule RT, crates/gravity/lint/rules/rt_thread_state.py, whose module doc is the
format): one file per source file (<path under crates/, '/' as '.'>), one row per thread-local static it declares,
<path> <static> <owner> <reset> <carry> [<member | note>]. OWNERS holds the owner tags. Every static in RT's scope
(every source under crates/, tests/ out; C7 coverage E2) has a row here, in ../TLS-DEBT or in ../SCOPE-DEBT.
The claim rows' members are checked against CLAIM_REGISTRY by hosts worker_arm.rs claim_census_is_pinned.

It replaced hosts/claim-census.tsv (C7 (b)/(c), carry rule only; deleted by the contract entry with RT's TRANSITION
clause and tools tls_census.py check_claim). Where each check of that census went (each moved one has a planted RT
selftest case, run.py --selftest):
  census check (hosts test claim_census_is_pinned = H, tools tls_census.py check_claim = T)  -> home now
  row shape: >= 3 fields, a known class (H, T)                     -> RT "carry .. is not one of" (planted4), row shape
  a claim row names its member (H, T)                              -> RT "names its CLAIM_REGISTRY member" (planted5)
  a debt row says what is missing (H, T)                           -> RT "names what is missing" (planted6)
  the claim row's member carries it (H)                            -> compiled half: claim_census_is_pinned
  two lines / two classes for one static (H, T)                    -> RT "two registry rows" (planted3)
  an unclassified static in the scope (H, T)                       -> RT "is in no registry row" (planted, planted8)
  a line whose static is gone (H, T)                               -> RT "no such thread-local in the scope" (planted2)
  the scope: #scope prefixes, tests/ out (H, T)                    -> RT SCOPE (planted7: out of scope = stale;
                                                                      planted8: a backend prefix needs a row; clean8: tests/)
  #carry-debt = the debt line count (H, T)                         -> RT: a carry debt row the parent lacks fails
                                                                      (planted9; CARRY-DEBT printed in RT's note)
  #scope / #carry-debt header lines present (H)                    -> no header now: the scope is RT's SCOPE
  each member's static is a thread-local (H)                       -> compiled half: claim_census_is_pinned
  a member's static with a row is classed claim (H)                -> compiled half (now TLS-DEBT rows too)
