Macro-declared thread-locals (C7 coverage E1, rt_thread_state.py module doc): each invocation entry of a thread-local
macro (scalar_global!, session_guc_*!) is a static of the invoking file, with its own row (planted26 an entry with no
row, planted28 an exported macro invoked in another file); the `$x` template is no static (planted27); a reset through
the entry's accessor holds, another entry's does not (planted29, clean13); a macro RT cannot read fails (planted30);
clean14 an invocation in another file with its rows.
The whole workspace (C7 coverage E2): a static of any crate needs a row (planted31; planted7 is now a row under tests/);
../SCOPE-DEBT holds the statics the widening found, only shrinks (planted32, clean15), goes when its static is registered
(planted33), has a row shape (planted34) and is no second debt row (planted35); a row whose static is gone is spent
(clean16). lint/reports/rt_scope_seed.py wrote the seed: unit-test module statics as owner unittest, test / test rows
(its --selftest: what proves a #[cfg(test)] parent), the rest as SCOPE-DEBT.
